-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6): one entry per declaration
-- (module parameters and instances included), naming the definitions its
-- step reads "by definition".  An empty entry: the step opens nothing.
-- Reviewed against the text (28 Oct 2026, handoff-2 §2b).  Kinds of entries:
--   the notion the step manipulates: isEquiv, Equiv, isContr, isProp, isSet,
--     isTrunc, isConn (reading .sec, .1, the suc case), fib, O2, subst at refl;
--   the declaration's own "by definition" lemmas (precomp-def, Y-def, ...);
--   numerals two .. five (suc n compared with a numeral);
--   library chains, read as one notion: PtMap -> PtSec; Maps.loop -> PMO;
--     HC -> STr.C -> Quot.Q -> Quot.image; Trunc.carrier -> Trunc.image;
--   library-side, known (§2c): PiOne.grp/O -> QGrp.G/grp -> Quot.Q in
--     ConnPi1 and the pi_1 lemmas (HomotopyGroups ind-*, LoopIso), and
--     Maps.D in c2, loop-ptid and the loop calculations of SphereAxiom.
-- Check: segd All.seg --opens FILE ; every line must say "nothing else opened".
